# Pi secrets catalog

Jarvis syncs machine-local secrets with the Raspberry Pi via `deploy/sync_secrets.py`, which reads **only** the catalog in `deploy/secret_paths.py`.

When you add a new secret or runtime file that must also live on the Pi (credential JSON, per-user YAML, DB, extra env file, etc.):

1. Add it to `SECRET_GROUPS` or `SECRET_GLOBS` in `deploy/secret_paths.py` in the **same** change.
2. Set `GROUP_POLICY` to `push` (credentials/bootstrap) or `sync` (live config that may change on the Pi).
3. Prefer a glob when many users/accounts share a pattern (see existing `user-prefs` / `google`).
4. Skip tracked templates (`example_user`, `*_example.json`).
5. If operators need to know about the asset, mention it in README “Local runtime assets”.
6. Extend `tests/test_deploy_secret_paths.py` when the new pattern is non-obvious.

Do not assume `sync_secrets` will pick up new paths automatically.
